  "comments": "House of Windsor (1917 to date), Elizabeth II (1952-2022), Pre-decimal issues (1953-70).<br /><br />\r\nThe standard weight of these coins was 4/11 troy ounce (174.5 grains). Under the Coinage Act of 1946, the composition changed from .500 silver to .750 copper/.250 nickel but the weight remained unchanged.<br /><br />\r\nThe 1970-dated proof strikes were issued as part of the &#039;Last Sterling&#039; mint set which comprised<br />\r\nhalf crown to halfpenny and were produced over the course of several years:<br />\r\n01/04/71-31/03/72 = 69,763<br />\r\n01/04/72-31/03/73 = 586,554<br />\r\n01/04/73-31/03/74 = 74,293<br />\r\n01/04/74-31/03/75 = 19,814",
